cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this method or these results, please cite this repository."
title: "Markerless footfall measurement from monocular video by static-scene reconstruction"
abstract: >-
  A pipeline that measures the ground contacts of a freely walking arthropod
  from a single handheld camera. Rather than reconstructing the deforming
  animal, it reconstructs the static scene with the animal masked out, which
  yields camera pose and a ground plane; a planted foot is then determined in
  closed form as the intersection of its optical ray with that plane.
type: software
